/* ============================================================
   THE INTERTESTAMENTAL ATLAS — 587 BC to 4 BC
   Persia, Alexander, the Ptolemies and Seleucids, the Maccabean
   revolt, the Hasmonean state, Pompey’s Rome and Herod.

   This file extends the Old Testament data rather than replacing
   it: places, eras, events, campaigns, finds, peoples, precision
   notes, chronology bands and rulers are pushed into the same
   arrays the atlas already draws from.

   Sources are named in each entry. Where the record is a single
   ancient historian (Josephus, 1–2 Maccabees, Polybius, Strabo)
   the entry says so; where a site is excavated, it says that too.
   Dates are BC throughout and follow the standard scholarly
   chronology of the Hellenistic and Roman east.
   ============================================================ */

